7.1 Scalability Strategy

For $N = 26$ satellites with $|\mathcal{Q}| = 4 \times 5 \times 3 \times 4 = 240$, the naive state space is $240^{26}$, infeasible. We adopt assume-guarantee contract decomposition following NASA practice: assume-guarantee contracts define expected behavior of systems, subsystems, and components, with assumptions or pre-conditions on the subsystem's inputs bounding the conditions in which the contract applies. Functionality is represented as a state machine using TLA⁺, and contracts are verified using TLC.

